Source published for reference under the Microsoft Reference Source License (Ms-RSL), copyright 2026 Jorian Burssens. The builds we publish (downloads, app stores, the Alnasl Pi image) may be used free of charge to run chess events; that permission covers our builds, not builds you make yourself.

The release machinery - rel/ (the Windows launcher and installer script, the
Linux installer, updater and systemd units, the macOS app and its build
scripts), .github/workflows, tools/release_notes.sh and the launcher details
endpoint (lib/ascella/launcher_details*, lib/ascella_web/plugs/
launcher_stats.ex) - came from Alnasl (https://github.com/teapot-chess/Alnasl),
by the same owner. Changes: the names
(Alnasl -> Ascella), the port, the parts that only make sense for a program
that reads boards over a serial port or keeps a database, and on Linux the
service, which runs as root here because installing other programs is its
job.

What the Windows downloads carry besides Ascella

   None of this is in the repository; the release workflow puts it in the
   installer and the zip.

   - Erlang/OTP's runtime (Apache-2.0) and the compiled dependencies listed
     in mix.lock, each under its own licence.
   - Velopack (https://github.com/velopack/velopack), MIT licence,
     Copyright (c) Velopack Ltd. and contributors: the installer and
     updater (Setup.exe, Update.exe, the stub beside them) and
     velopack_libc.dll, which the launcher loads to apply an update.
     rel/windows/launcher.c declares the part of its C interface it calls.
   - Microsoft's Visual C++ runtime (vcruntime140.dll, vcruntime140_1.dll,
     msvcp140.dll), which Erlang's Windows build needs, redistributed
     unchanged beside it as Microsoft's terms for those files allow.
